 the recalibrated variant is largest on forest (0.0054 against 0.0168) and alphafold (0.0038 against 0.0104), whose ceilings are unknown. On the search synthetic family, which has a nonlinear regime, the two variants are close (0.0707 against 0.0757). The paper also states that these are single evaluations that differ in several components and cannot isolate a mechanism.\n  - claim: The more elaborate stack did not beat the simpler recalibrated interval on the aggregate, \"which is consistent with the headroom analysis: when the ceiling is small, richer calibrators have little to gain and pay an estimation cost.\"\n  - evidence: analysis/headroom_derived.json keys cover only real.census_income, census_healthcare, census_education, plankton and the sealed synthetic regimes; source_evidence/search_metrics/recalibrated_metrics.json and stacked_metrics.json per-family log ratios; paper.tex Section 5.4 and Table tab:search.\n  - requested_fix: Delete the \"consistent with the headroom analysis\" explanation. State only that the stacked variant scored lower on the aggregate (0.0223 against 0.0271) in single, uncontrolled evaluations, and that no search-pool ceilings were computed.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[0].font_sizes.title below minimum: 8.5 < 10.0\n- figures[0].font_sizes.axis below minimum: 8.5 < 9.0\n- figures[0].font_sizes.legend below minimum: 7.5 < 8.0\n- figures[1] exceeds series budget in panel 0: 2 > 1\n- figures[1] exceeds series budget in panel 1: 2 > 1\n- figures[1].font_sizes.title below minimum: 8.5 < 10.0\n- figures[1].font_sizes.axis below minimum: 8.5 < 9.0\n- figures[1].font_sizes.legend below minimum: 7.5 < 8.0\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1717 < 2400\n- figures[2].font_sizes.title below minimum: 8.5 < 10.0\n- figures[2].font_sizes.axis below minimum: 8.5 < 9.0\n- figures[2].font_sizes.legend below minimum: 7.5 < 8.0\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1654 < 2400\n- figures[3].font_sizes.title below minimum: 8.5 < 10.0\n- figures[3].font_s